## ==============================================================================
## local.properties.example — Honeypot Android Application
## ==============================================================================
## This is a template configuration file for local developer machine setup.
##
## HOW TO USE:
## 1. Copy or rename this file to "local.properties" in the project root:
##      cp local.properties.example local.properties
## 2. Fill in your Android SDK path and optional API keys below.
## 3. Note: "local.properties" is in .gitignore and will NEVER be committed to Git.
## ==============================================================================

## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 1. Android SDK Location (Required for Gradle build)
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Path to your Android SDK installation.
##
## Windows example (note double backslashes and escaped colon):
##   sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\YourUsername\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
##
## macOS / Linux example:
##   sdk.dir=/Users/YourUsername/Library/Android/sdk
##
sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\Harshal\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk


## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 2. Google Gemini API Key (Optional — Cloud AI Reply & Reasoning)
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Powers cloud-based generative honeypot replies and first-message threat
## reasoning via Gemini 1.5 / 2.0 Flash API.
##
## HOW TO GET A FREE KEY:
## 1. Visit Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/
## 2. Sign in with your Google account.
## 3. Click "Get API key" -> "Create API key".
## 4. Copy the key and paste it below.
##
## NOTE: If this key is blank or omitted, the application automatically uses
## the on-device deterministic ReplyProgressionEngine (offline question banks)
## with zero loss of core scam detection functionality.
##
GEMINI_API_KEY=


## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 3. Google Safe Browsing API Key (Optional — URL Threat Verification)
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Powers real-time URL threat checks for suspicious links found in scam SMS.
##
## HOW TO GET A FREE KEY:
## 1. Visit Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
## 2. Create or select a project.
## 3. Navigate to "APIs & Services" -> "Library".
## 4. Search for "Safe Browsing API" (v4) and click "Enable".
## 5. Navigate to "APIs & Services" -> "Credentials".
## 6. Click "+ CREATE CREDENTIALS" -> "API key".
## 7. Copy the key and paste it below.
##
## NOTE: If this key is blank or omitted, URL checking is gracefully skipped
## and URLs are evaluated by regex and indicator rules only.
##
SAFE_BROWSING_API_KEY=
